 The rotation matrix for an angle $\theta$ clockwise is given by: \[
R = \begin{pmatrix}
\cos(\theta) & \sin(\theta) \\
-\sin(\theta) & \cos(\theta)
\end{pmatrix}
\]
For $\theta = 45^\circ$, we have:
\[
\cos(45^\circ) = \sin(45^\circ) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}
\]
